{"name":"India Ink","hex":"#3c3d4c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"india","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of India of the ICAO/NATO radiotelephony alphabet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of India from the NATO/ICAO Phonetic Alphabet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/india"},{"term":"ink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigment (or dye)-based fluid used for writing, printing etc.","A particular type, color or container of this fluid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply ink to; to cover or smear with ink.","To sign (a contract or similar document)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ink"}],"entries":[{"title":"India ink","blocks":[{"text":"India ink or China ink is a simple black or coloured ink once widely used for writing and printing and now more commonly used for drawing and outlining, especially when inking comic books and comic strips. India ink is also used in medical applications."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/New_Edition_with_Supplemental_Annotations_of_The_Inner_Canon_of_the_Yellow_Emperor._Su_wen_WDL11409.jpg/330px-New_Edition_with_Supplemental_Annotations_of_The_Inner_Canon_of_the_Yellow_Emperor._Su_wen_WDL11409.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India_ink","wikidata":"Q12981547"},{"title":"India","blocks":[{"text":"India, officially the Republic of India, is a country in South Asia. It is the world's seventh-largest country by area and its most populous. Bounded by the Indian Ocean on the south, the Arabian Sea on the southwest, and the Bay of Bengal on the southeast, it shares land borders with Pakistan to the west, China, Nepal, and Bhutan to the north, and Bangladesh and Myanmar to the east. In the Indian Ocean, India is near Sri Lanka and the Maldives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/41/Flag_of_India.svg/330px-Flag_of_India.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India","wikidata":"Q668"},{"title":"Ink","blocks":[{"text":"Ink is a gel, sol, or solution that contains at least one colorant, such as a dye or pigment, and is used to color a surface to produce an image, text, or design. Ink is used for drawing or writing with a pen, brush, reed pen, or quill. Thicker inks, in paste form, are used extensively in letterpress and lithographic printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg/330px-F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ink","wikidata":"Q127418"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Inkstick.jpg/500px-Inkstick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Inkstick.jpg/500px-Inkstick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A solid ink stick used for the preparation of ink","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInkstick.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Inkmaking_-_Tiangong_Kaiwu.jpg/500px-Inkmaking_-_Tiangong_Kaiwu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Inkmaking_-_Tiangong_Kaiwu.jpg/1280px-Inkmaking_-_Tiangong_Kaiwu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Inkmaking_-_Tiangong_Kaiwu.jpg/500px-Inkmaking_-_Tiangong_Kaiwu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inkmaking from pine wood, as depicted in the Tiangong Kaiwu (1637)","link":"ht